<title>USA: Glickman meeting with Turkish ambassador today.</title>
<headline>Glickman meeting with Turkish ambassador today.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Friday he will meet the Turkish ambassador this morning to discuss the current controversy over grain imports to Turkey.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a concern for us,&quot; said Glickman.</p>
<p>USDA has stopped issuing export certificates for all grains and oilseed shipments to Turkey due to recent implementation by Turkey of strict import regulations.</p>
<p>The issue flared up two weeks ago when Turkey began requiring a zero-tolerance level in wheat for the ergot disease. Turkey said earlier this week that it would raise its tolerance level for ergot to 0.02 percent, but USDA officials said that is still too low. Turkey also notified USDA that it would impose zero-tolerance levels on a host of other diseases impacting most of the grains and oilseeds that the United States exports to that nation.</p>
</text>
